      "message": "**Feedback:** Rather than writing out the ceiling division math `(A + B - 1) / B` manually in multiple places, let\u0027s create a standard helper function. This makes the code\u0027s intent instantly readable and prevents accidental order-of-operations bugs.\n\n**1\\. Add the inline function to a header (e.g., `ff_util.h`):**\n\n```c\n/* Safely calculates the ceiling division of n / d */\nstatic inline uint32_t ft_div_round_up(uint32_t n, uint32_t d) \n{\n\treturn (n + d - 1) / d;\n}\n\n```\n\n*(Note: You can also implement this as a type-agnostic macro `#define FT_DIV_ROUND_UP(n, d) (((n) + (d) - 1) / (d))`, which is the standard approach in the Linux kernel.)*\n\n**2\\. Update `ft_erase_page` in `fun.c`:**\n\n```c\n\t/* Old */\n\t// count \u003d (length + FOCAL_CONFIG_SIZE - 1) / FOCAL_CONFIG_SIZE;\n\n\t/* New */\n\tcount \u003d ft_div_round_up(length, FOCAL_CONFIG_SIZE);\n\n```\n\n**3\\. Update `ft_download_bin` in `fun.c`:**\n\n```c\n\t/* Old */\n\t// total_frame \u003d file_len / FOCAL_CONFIG_SIZE;\n\t// if (file_len % FOCAL_CONFIG_SIZE)\n\t// \ttotal_frame++;\n\n\t/* New */\n\ttotal_frame \u003d ft_div_round_up(file_len, FOCAL_CONFIG_SIZE);\n\n```",
