      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T20:24:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Feedback:** The `ff_util_hexdump` function contains deeply nested formatting logic and manual ASCII range checking (`buf[i] \u003e\u003d 0x20 \u0026\u0026 buf[i] \u003c 0x7F`). You can remove the need for `tmp_buf` and simplify the logic by using standard library features like `isprint()` from `\u003cctype.h\u003e` and processing the buffer in 16-byte chunks.\n\nThe following code was generated by Gemini so double-check for correctness:\n\n-----\n\n**Suggested Rewrite:**\n\n```c\n#include \u003cctype.h\u003e\n#include \u003cstdint.h\u003e\n#include \u003cstdio.h\u003e\n\nvoid ff_util_hexdump(uint8_t mak, const char *info, const uint8_t *buf, uint32_t len)\n{\n\tif (!mak || len \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\treturn;\n\t}\n\n\tif (info) {\n\t\tprintf(\"%s: length \u003d %u [0x%X]\\r\\n\", info, len, len);\n\t}\n\n\tfor (uint32_t i \u003d 0; i \u003c len; i +\u003d 16) {\n\t\t/* Print memory address */\n\t\tprintf(\"%p  \", (void *)(buf + i));\n\n\t\t/* Print hex values (with padding for partial lines) */\n\t\tfor (uint32_t j \u003d 0; j \u003c 16; j++) {\n\t\t\tif (i + j \u003c len) {\n\t\t\t\tprintf(\"%02X \", buf[i + j]);\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tprintf(\"   \"); /* Pad missing hex bytes */\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tif (j \u003d\u003d 7) {\n\t\t\t\tprintf(\"- \"); /* 8-byte separator */\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tprintf(\"  | \");\n\n\t\t/* Print ASCII representation */\n\t\tfor (uint32_t j \u003d 0; j \u003c 16 \u0026\u0026 (i + j) \u003c len; j++) {\n\t\t\tuint8_t c \u003d buf[i + j];\n\t\t\tputchar(isprint(c) ? c : \u0027.\u0027);\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tprintf(\"\\r\\n\");\n\t}\n}\n\n```\n\n### Why this is better:\n\n1. **Removes `tmp_buf` state management:** By iterating 16 bytes at a time, you can loop once for the hex output and a second time (inside the chunk) for the ASCII output, completely eliminating the need to buffer the string.  \n2. **Standard Library usage:** `isprint()` natively handles printable character checks, replacing magic number bounds checking.  \n3. **Flattens the logic:** Removes the nested `if/else if` blocks checking `len % 16` and `i % 8`, dropping the cyclomatic complexity.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 71
      },
