      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Potential Infinite Loop via Integer Overflow**\n\nThe loop counter `i` is declared as a `uint16_t`, but the input `len` is a `uint32_t`. If `ff_util_hexdump` is ever called with a `len` greater than 65535, `i` will overflow and wrap around to 0 before ever reaching `len`, resulting in an infinite loop.\n\n**Remediation:** Change the type of `i` to `uint32_t` to match the type of `len`.",
      "revId": "fcd9064294552a3cbf330ce87121caabb6c418c8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
