      "message": "* **Print Formats:** In `ff_util.c`, `printf(\"%p  \", addr);` prints pointers. On a 64-bit host, this prints 16 characters (plus `0x`), misaligning the hex dump layout which seems tightly coded to assume specific column widths. Consider using `%08lX` cast to an integer type if fixed-width alignment is strictly required.",
