      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T20:49:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `log_printf`, the code calls `vsnprintf(buf, LOG_BUF_SIZE - 1, fmt, ap);`.\n\n**Feedback:** Subtracting `1` from the buffer size is a legacy anti-pattern from older, non-standard string functions. The standard C `vsnprintf` takes the **total size of the buffer** and guarantees it will write at most `size - 1` characters and append a null terminator. By passing `LOG_BUF_SIZE - 1`, you are permanently leaving the last byte of the buffer unused.\n\n* **Recommendation:** Pass the full size: `vsnprintf(buf, sizeof(buf), fmt, ap);`.",
