      "message": "The logging function uses a chained `if/else if` block to determine the ANSI color code based on the log level. This can be simplified into a simple lookup array, matching the existing `log_level_char` array pattern.\n\n**Current Code:**\n\n```c\nif (level \u003d\u003d LOG_LEVEL_ERR) {\n\tprintf(\"\\033[31m[%s] %c [%s] %s \\033[0m\\n\", time_buff, log_level_char[level], tag, buf);\n} else if (level \u003d\u003d LOG_LEVEL_WRN) {\n\tprintf(\"\\033[33m[%s] %c [%s] %s \\033[0m\\n\", time_buff, log_level_char[level], tag, buf);\n} // ...\n\n```\n\n**Suggested Rewrite:** Use an array of color prefixes mapped to the `log_level_t` enum.\n\n```c\nstatic const char *log_colors[] \u003d {\n\t\"\",         /* ALL - no color */\n\t\"\",         /* VBS */\n\t\"\",         /* DBG */\n\t\"\\033[36m\", /* INF - Cyan */\n\t\"\\033[33m\", /* WRN - Yellow */\n\t\"\\033[31m\"  /* ERR - Red */\n};\n\n/* Inside log_printf: */\nconst char *color \u003d (level \u003c\u003d LOG_LEVEL_ERR) ? log_colors[level] : \"\";\nconst char *reset \u003d (color[0] !\u003d \u0027\\0\u0027) ? \"\\033[0m\" : \"\";\n\nprintf(\"%s[%s] %c [%s] %s %s\\n\", color, time_buff, log_level_char[level], tag, buf, reset);\n\n```",
