      "message": "* **Hardcoded USB Interface Claim (`ft_sg_io.c`):** In `ft_sg_open`, the code correctly iterates over the USB configurations to dynamically find the Mass Storage Class (MSC) interface. However, it later ignores this discovery and hardcodes `libusb_claim_interface(dev_handle, 0);`. If the MSC interface happens to be `1` (or anything else), this will fail.  \n    \n* *Suggestion:* Save the interface number during discovery (`int msc_iface \u003d iface_desc-\u003ebInterfaceNumber;`) and use `libusb_claim_interface(dev_handle, msc_iface);`.",
