      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Feedback:** Similar to the connection function, the interface iteration loop nests 5 levels deep. By inverting the `if` conditions and using `continue`, we can keep the logic closer to the left margin.\n\nThe following was generated by Gemini so double-check for correctness:\n\n-----\n\n**Suggested Rewrite:**\n\n```c\n\tfor (int i \u003d 0; i \u003c config-\u003ebNumInterfaces; i++) {\n\t\tconst struct libusb_interface *interface \u003d \u0026config-\u003einterface[i];\n\t\tfor (int j \u003d 0; j \u003c interface-\u003enum_altsetting; j++) {\n\t\t\tconst struct libusb_interface_descriptor *iface_desc \u003d \u0026interface-\u003ealtsetting[j];\n\t\t\t\n\t\t\t/* Guard clause: Skip non-MSC interfaces */\n\t\t\tif (iface_desc-\u003ebInterfaceClass !\u003d LIBUSB_CLASS_MASS_STORAGE) {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue;\n\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\tfound_msc \u003d 1;\n\n\t\t\tfor (int k \u003d 0; k \u003c iface_desc-\u003ebNumEndpoints; k++) {\n\t\t\t\tconst struct libusb_endpoint_descriptor *ep \u003d \u0026iface_desc-\u003eendpoint[k];\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t/* Guard clause: Skip non-bulk endpoints */\n\t\t\t\tif (ep-\u003ebmAttributes !\u003d LIBUSB_ENDPOINT_TRANSFER_TYPE_BULK) {\n\t\t\t\t\tcontinue;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\n\t\t\t\tif ((ep-\u003ebEndpointAddress \u0026 LIBUSB_ENDPOINT_DIR_MASK) \u003d\u003d LIBUSB_ENDPOINT_IN) {\n\t\t\t\t\tg_ft_boot_ep.ep_bulk_in \u003d ep-\u003ebEndpointAddress;\n\t\t\t\t} else if ((ep-\u003ebEndpointAddress \u0026 LIBUSB_ENDPOINT_DIR_MASK) \u003d\u003d LIBUSB_ENDPOINT_OUT) {\n\t\t\t\t\tg_ft_boot_ep.ep_bulk_out \u003d ep-\u003ebEndpointAddress;\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n```",
