      "side": 1,
      "message": "The codebase currently maintains two identical macros for the SCSI command length, and mixes them indiscriminately in `fun.c`:\n\n* `#define FT_CMD_LENGTH 16` (in `ff_sg_io.h`)  \n* `#define CMD_LENGTH 0x10` (in `fun.c`)\n\n**Feedback:** Remove `#define CMD_LENGTH 0x10` from `fun.c` entirely. Standardize on `FT_CMD_LENGTH` everywhere to avoid confusing maintainers who might assume they represent different buffer sizes.",
