      "message": "`fun.c` defines a custom `U32_SET` macro to manually extract and shift bytes into a buffer in Little-Endian format:\n\n```c\n#define U32_SET(buf, u) \\\n\t(buf)[3] \u003d (unsigned char)((u) \u003e\u003e 24); \\\n\t/* ... etc ... */\n\n```\n\n**Feedback:** Since you are already using `#include \u003cendian.h\u003e` and `htole32()` in `ft_sg_io.c`, you shouldn\u0027t reinvent the wheel in `fun.c`. The standard library handles this safely and often more efficiently via compiler intrinsics.\n\n* **Recommendation:** Remove `U32_SET`. You can easily replace it using standard functions:\n\n```c\n/* Instead of: U32_SET(\u0026transfer_cmd[1], addr); */\nuint32_t le_addr \u003d htole32(addr);\nmemcpy(\u0026transfer_cmd[1], \u0026le_addr, sizeof(le_addr));\n\n```",
