      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Crash Risk: `fclose(NULL)`**\n\nIf `fopen()` fails to open the file, it returns `NULL`, and the code jumps to `goto exit;`.\nAt the `exit:` label, `fclose(file)` is called unconditionally. Passing a `NULL` pointer to `fclose()` causes undefined behavior, which on most systems will result in an immediate segmentation fault.\n\n**Remediation:** Add a null check before closing:\n```c\nif (file) {\n    fclose(file);\n}\n```\n*(Note: This exact same bug exists in `ft_verify_data()` at line 448).*",
