      "side": 1,
      "message": "At the end of `ft_verify_data`, if the hash comparison fails, the code manually sets the return value and jumps to `exit`.\n\n**Current Code:**\n\n```c\n\tif (memcmp(pHash, read_hash, SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH)) {\n\t\tFF_LOGE(\"verify error!\");\n\t\t// ... logs ...\n\t\tret_value \u003d FT_RESULT_FAIL;\n\t\tgoto exit;\n\t}\n\nexit:\n\n```\n\nSince this is literally the last block of code before the `exit` label, jumping is redundant. You can let it naturally fall through to the cleanup block.\n\n**Suggested Rewrite:**\n\n```c\n\tif (memcmp(pHash, read_hash, SHA256_DIGEST_LENGTH)) {\n\t\tFF_LOGE(\"verify error!\");\n\t\t// ... logs ...\n\t\tret_value \u003d FT_RESULT_FAIL;\n\t}\n\n\t/* Natural fallthrough to cleanup */\n\tif (file) fclose(file);\n\tif (buffer) free(buffer);\n\n\treturn ret_value;\n\n```",
