      "writtenOn": "2026-05-08T20:36:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `goto` pattern is excellent for centralizing resource cleanup . However, in `ft_disboot` and `ft_download_page`, there are no dynamically allocated resources, locks, or open files to clean up. The `exit` label simply returns the error code.\n\nUsing `goto exit` here just adds visual noise and forces the reader to jump to the bottom of the function to see what happens.\n\n**Current Code (`ft_disboot`):**\n\n```c\n\tret_value \u003d usb_write(write_disbootdata_cmd, CMD_LENGTH, disbootdata,\n\t\t\t      disbootlen, WRITE_DATA_TO_USB);\n\tif (ret_value) {\n\t\tFF_LOGE(\"write disbootdata error!\");\n\t\tgoto exit;\n\t}\n// ...\nexit:\n\treturn ret_value;\n\n```\n\n**Suggested Rewrite:**\nRemove the `exit` label entirely and return immediately upon failure. This makes the functions strictly linear and easier to trace.\n\n```c\n\tret_value \u003d usb_write(write_disbootdata_cmd, CMD_LENGTH, disbootdata,\n\t\t\t      disbootlen, WRITE_DATA_TO_USB);\n\tif (ret_value) {\n\t\tFF_LOGE(\"write disbootdata error!\");\n\t\treturn ret_value;\n\t}\n\n```\n\n*(Apply this exact same simplification to `ft_download_page` as well).*",
