      "message": "* **Misleading Return Semantics (`fun.c`):** `is_ec_bin_has_config_page` conflates `FT_SUCCESS` (which evaluates to `0` or falsy) with a \"false\" state if the file cannot be opened. While it happens to work functionally (because 0 translates to \"no config page\"), it is semantically confusing.  \n    \n* *Suggestion:* Have boolean-like functions return `true`/`false` (`\u003cstdbool.h\u003e` is already included) and handle file read errors distinctly from finding/not finding the config page.",
