      "message": "When allocating memory or clearing a pointer\u0027s destination, it is safer and more idiomatic to use `sizeof(*pointer)` rather than explicitly naming the type `sizeof(Type)`. If the type of the pointer ever changes during refactoring, `sizeof(*pointer)` automatically adapts, preventing buffer overflows.\n\n**Current Code (`ft_device_init`):**\n\n```c\n\tif (info) {\n\t\tmemset(info, 0, sizeof(ft_device_info_t));\n\n```\n\n**Suggested Rewrite:**\n\n```c\n\tif (info) {\n\t\tmemset(info, 0, sizeof(*info));\n\n```",
