      "message": "**Feedback:** The `LIBUSB_HOTPLUG_EVENT_DEVICE_ARRIVED` branch uses an `else` block that holds the entire initialization logic, which further nests more `if` statements. Handling the `DEVICE_LEFT` event first and using early returns removes the need for `else` branches entirely.\n\nThe following was generated by Gemini, so review for correctness:\n\n-----\n\n**Suggested Rewrite:**\n\n```c\n\tif (LIBUSB_HOTPLUG_EVENT_DEVICE_LEFT \u003d\u003d event) {\n\t\tFF_LOGW(\"usb device removed: %04x:%04x\", desc.idVendor, desc.idProduct);\n\n\t\tif (ret) {\n\t\t\t*ret \u003d FT_USB_DEVICE_REMOVE_MAGIC;\n\t\t}\n\n\t\tif (usb_ctx-\u003ehandle) {\n\t\t\tlibusb_free_device_list(usb_ctx-\u003edevs, 1);\n\t\t\tlibusb_release_interface(usb_ctx-\u003ehandle, 0);\n\t\t\tlibusb_close(usb_ctx-\u003ehandle);\n\t\t\tusb_ctx-\u003ehandle \u003d NULL;\n\t\t\tg_no_device_flag \u003d 0;\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn FT_SUCCESS;\n\t}\n\n\tif (LIBUSB_HOTPLUG_EVENT_DEVICE_ARRIVED !\u003d event) {\n\t\treturn FT_SUCCESS;\n\t}\n\n\tFF_LOGD(\"usb device attached: %04x:%04x\", desc.idVendor, desc.idProduct);\n\n\tif (usb_ctx-\u003ehandle) {\n\t\tlibusb_close(usb_ctx-\u003ehandle);\n\t\tusb_ctx-\u003ehandle \u003d NULL;\n\t}\n\n\tr \u003d libusb_open(dev, \u0026usb_ctx-\u003ehandle);\n\tif (LIBUSB_SUCCESS !\u003d r) {\n\t\tFF_LOGE(\"error opening device.\");\n\t\treturn FT_SUCCESS; \n\t}\n\n\tif (libusb_kernel_driver_active(usb_ctx-\u003ehandle, 0) \u003d\u003d 1) {\n\t\tFF_LOGD(\"kernel driver active\");\n\t\tif (libusb_detach_kernel_driver(usb_ctx-\u003ehandle, 0) \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\t\tFF_LOGD(\"kernel driver detach\");\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\tr \u003d libusb_claim_interface(usb_ctx-\u003ehandle, 0); \n\tif (r \u003c 0) {\n\t\tFF_LOGE(\"libusb_claim_interface failed: %s\", libusb_error_name(r));\n\t\treturn FT_NO_SUCH_DEV;\n\t}\n\t\n\tg_no_device_flag \u003d 1;\n\tFF_LOGD(\"usb device open success %p\", usb_ctx-\u003ehandle);\n\t\n\treturn FT_SUCCESS;\n\n```",
